<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/20th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Treaty</p><h1 class="enc-title">Treaty of Kyakhta (1915)</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1915">1915</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Also known as Kyakhta Agreement</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Treaty of Kyakhta of 1915 was a tripartite agreement between <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/russia">Russia</a>, the Republic of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/china">China</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mongolia">Mongolia</a>, signed at the border town of Kyakhta in June 1915. It reduced the Bogd Khanate, which had declared independence in 1911, to an autonomous <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/outer-mongolia">Outer Mongolia</a> under Chinese suzerainty, while Russia kept its economic rights. China abolished the autonomy in 1919.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/treaty-of-kyakhta-1915.jpg" alt="Treaty of Kyakhta (1915)" width="320" height="261" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:%E4%B8%AD%E4%BF%84%E8%92%99%E5%8D%8F%E7%BA%A6%E7%AD%BE%E8%AE%A2%E7%8E%B0%E5%9C%BA.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
